msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/generalizing-ownership.md:43
msgid ""
"This example re-frames the borrow checker rules away from references and "
"towards semantic meaning in non-memory-safety settings."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/generalizing-ownership.md:46
msgid "Nothing is being mutated, nothing is being sent across threads."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/generalizing-ownership.md:48
msgid ""
"In Rust's borrow checker we have access to three different ways of "
"\"taking\" a value:"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/generalizing-ownership.md:51
msgid ""
"Owned value `T`. Value is dropped when the scope ends, unless it is not "
"returned to another scope."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/generalizing-ownership.md:54
msgid ""
"Shared Reference `&T`. Allows aliasing but prevents mutable access while "
"shared references are in use."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/generalizing-ownership.md:57
msgid ""
"Mutable Reference `&mut T`. Only one of these is allowed to exist for a "
"value at any one point, but can be used to create shared references."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/generalizing-ownership.md:60
msgid ""
"Ask: The two commented-out lines in the `demo` functions would cause "
"compilation errors, Why?"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/generalizing-ownership.md:63
msgid ""
"`demo_exclusive`: Because the `shared` value is still aliased after the "
"`exclusive` reference is taken."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/generalizing-ownership.md:66
msgid ""
"`demo_denied`: Because `value` is consumed the line before the "
"`shared_again_again` reference is taken from `&value`."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/generalizing-ownership.md:69
msgid ""
"Remember that every `&T` and `&mut T` has a lifetime, just one the user "
"doesn't have to annotate or think about most of the time."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/generalizing-ownership.md:72
msgid ""
"We rarely specify lifetimes because the Rust compiler allows us to _elide_ "
"them in most cases. See: [Lifetime Elision](../../../lifetimes/lifetime-"
"elision.md)"
msgstr ""
